  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\na\u00f7b=\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}\u00f7\\frac{12g}{7h},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}\u00f7\\frac{12g}{7h} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{7h}{12g} & = \\\\ \\frac{4g\\cdot g}{7h\\cdot {h}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{7h}{3\\cdot 4g} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4g}\\cdot g}{\\cancel{7h}\\cdot {h}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{7h}}{3\\cdot \\cancel{4g}} & = \\\\ \\frac{g}{3{h}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
